c(95, "§4.1 Interpretation — a crash on launch shipped at the exact moment a paid-acquisition or viral campaign drove installs (causation not established); the coincidence converted the largest-ever audience into the largest-ever pile of 1★: 35% of lifetime 1★ in 25 days; the 2022 mean of 1.74 is substantially a release-engineering outcome, not a product-concept verdict", "tactic",
  "Outcome of shipping a launch crash during an install surge: a crash on launch shipped at the exact moment a paid-acquisition or viral (TikTok) campaign was driving installs — the corpus cannot establish causation — and the coincidence converted the app's largest-ever audience into its largest-ever pile of 1★ reviews, 35% of lifetime 1★ in 25 days; the 2022 mean of 1.74 is therefore substantially a release-engineering outcome, not a product-concept verdict — freeze releases or stage rollouts before and during a campaign",
  "released v1.19.0 into a TikTok surge", "1★-burst", "35% of lifetime 1★ in 25 days; 2022 mean 1.74", "must-never-break", "interpretation", "yes", [])
