  "A 2–3 item cap blocks evaluation, not just use: present in all eras at 8–18% (2 items in 2016, then 3); 'Ready and willing to pay, but I'd first like to try it more. With only 2 items makes it hard to get a feel' — while a minority defend it as focus: 'it made me prioritise'; 'if you've read The One Thing, three is already a lot!'; 'two (three, actually) habits at a time seem like the perfect amount'; '3 goal tracking … is plenty for me'",
